  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Initial Access — External Remote Services (TCP/3389 reachability probe)", "technique": "T1133", "what_happened": "At 2026-04-19 02:14:08 UTC, Sysmon Event 3 (network connection) on agent WIN-DMZ-RDP01 (10.108.57.177) recorded an inbound TCP connection to local port 3389 with data.win.eventdata.ipAddress=45.155.205.112 — a public IP. RDP/3389 is directly reachable from the Internet on this host. Suricata corroborated with a flow alert on data.dstport=3389 from data.srcip=45.155.205.112. The fact that an external public IP can open a TCP session to 3389 at all is the structural exposure that makes every subsequent step possible.", "chain_reason": "Sysmon EID 3 with data.win.eventdata.ipAddress=45.155.205.112 (public) to destination port 3389, plus Suricata flow with data.srcip=45.155.205.112 / data.dstport=3389. External-to-3389 reachability is the precondition for the auth attempts that follow.", "first_seen": "2026-04-19T02:14:08+0000"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Credential Access — Brute Force over RDP (failed logons)", "technique": "T1110", "what_happened": "Between 02:15:30 and 02:23:10 UTC, Windows Security logged three EventID 4625 (logon failure) events on WIN-DMZ-RDP01 with data.win.eventdata.logonType=10 (RemoteInteractive / RDP) and data.win.eventdata.ipAddress=45.155.205.112. The three failures targeted three different accounts — alice, administrator, and contractor.smith — at ~90s intervals. Same external source, RDP logon type, multiple accounts = a low-and-slow credential-spray pattern against the exposed RDP endpoint.", "chain_reason": "Three data.win.eventdata.logonType=10 EventID 4625 failures from the SAME data.win.eventdata.ipAddress=45.155.205.112 against three distinct data.win.eventdata.targetUserName values within an 8-minute window. Wazuh rule 5710/5760 correlation (RDP authentication failure from external IP / multiple RDP failures from same source) fired.", "first_seen": "2026-04-19T02:15:30+0000"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Initial Access — Valid Accounts over External Remote Services (successful RDP logon)", "technique": "T1021.001", "what_happened": "At 02:24:55 UTC — ~100 seconds after the third failed attempt — Windows Security logged EventID 4624 (logon success) on WIN-DMZ-RDP01 with data.win.eventdata.logonType=10 and data.win.eventdata.ipAddress=45.155.205.112, targetUserName=contractor.smith. The same account that failed at step 2 succeeded on the next attempt: the attacker found the working password. A successful RemoteInteractive logon directly from a public IP, immediately after a failed-spray burst from the SAME IP, is the canonical External Remote Services compromise — valid credentials over an Internet-exposed RDP service.", "chain_reason": "EventID 4624 with data.win.eventdata.logonType=10 and data.win.eventdata.ipAddress=45.155.205.112, targetUserName=contractor.smith, ~100s after the matching 4625 failure for the same account from the same source. Failure-then-success from one external IP against one account = brute-force success / credential compromise.", "first_seen": "2026-04-19T02:24:55+0000"}
  ],
